load("@rules_helm_img//:helm_oci_manifest.bzl", "helm_oci_manifest") helm_oci_manifest(*, name, chart, registry_url, registry_url_file, visibility, **kwargs) Describe a chart as the OCI artifact helm push creates, for rules_img's multi_deploy. The target is an image_manifest that provides DeployInfo, so it can be listed in the operations of a multi_deploy . Running the multi_deploy pushes the chart to <registry_url>/<chart name>:<chart version>, with + in the version replaced by _, as helm push would. Only the chart is pushed; push its images with their own targets. load("@rules_helm_img//:defs.bzl", "helm_oci_manifest")
load("@rules_img//img:multi_deploy.bzl", "multi_deploy") helm_oci_manifest( name = "my_chart_oci_manifest", chart = ":my_chart", registry_url = "oci://registry.example.com/charts",
) multi_deploy( name = "deploy", operations = [":my_chart_oci_manifest"],
) The pushed manifest is the one helm push creates when it runs in UTC, so its digest is the one helm_oci_digest gives. Helm writes the org.opencontainers.image.created annotation in the local time zone, so helm push in another zone pushes a different digest for the same chart. Compared with helm_push : Only oci:// registries are supported, so push_cmd and plugins such as cm-push are not. Registry credentials come from rules_img (Docker config and credential helpers), not from the HELM_REGISTRY_* variables (HELM_REGISTRY_USERNAME, HELM_REGISTRY_PASSWORD and HELM_REGISTRY_PASSWORD_FILE). There is no include_images. rules_img expands Go templates in annotation values. {{ in a chart's metadata is escaped, so the annotations match the chart. target rule {name} image_manifest {name}.oci_digest helm_oci_digest {name}.files config blob, annotations, tag, repository and layer files {name}.layer layer_from_file {name}.push_spec image_push_spec PARAMETERS Name Description Default Value name The name of the image_manifest target. none chart A helm_chart or helm_package target. Charts from helm_import are not supported. none registry_url The registry URL given to helm push, for example oci://registry.example.com/charts. Mutually exclusive with registry_url_file. None registry_url_file A file containing the registry URL. Mutually exclusive with registry_url. None visibility The visibility of {name}. The other targets are private. None kwargs Common attributes such as tags, target_compatible_with and testonly, applied to every target. none
